andrew mak <aom@melb.alexia.net.au> writes:
>Can anyone tell me where can I get a copy of TOP which will 
>compile under OSF/1? I have tried TOP3.2 and TOP3.3, but they 
>won't compil under OSF/1. Any idea?

Here's a poor man's "top".

#!/bin/sh
while true; do
	clear
	cat << EOF
USER       PID %CPU        TIME %MEM   VSZ  RSS TTY      S    COMMAND
EOF
	ps ax -o user,pid,pcpu,time,pmem,vsz,rss,tty,state,comm |
	sort -rn +2 +4 | head -20
	sleep 5
done

