This problem has been corrected in ladebug version 4.0-8.  There was a problem
with ladebug reading in partially, or fully stripped binaries, or binaries which
were not compiled with -g.  4.0-8 and later versions have corrected this problem.
As a workaround, you might try using the -nosharedobjs switch to ladebug on
startup.  This will prevent ladebug from reading those libraries which it is
choking on.

> Also, is there a decladebug.el that is compatible with emacs 19.30?
> I get the error: Symbol's function definition is void: gud-overload-functions

Yes, there is a new file, ladebug.el, which works with all known versions of
GNU Emacs.  It will be released with Digital UNIX 4.0 in the ladebug kit, but it
will work on any version of Digital UNIX that runs emacs.  If there is an urgent
need for it, send me mail.  I will also consider posting it here.

