In article <yfs20ne99ts.fsf@jupiter.SLAC.Stanford.EDU> raines@jupiter.slac.stanford.edu (Paul E. Raines) writes:

  >>>  To port some code from AIX, we wish to use 32-bit pointers. The
  >>> C compiler appears to provide the -xtaso_short flag for this.
  >>> We have found several problems with it. One is that it does not
  >>> seem to be consistant. Here is the output of a simple program to
  >>> print the size of objects. Note that witht he -xtaso_short flag,
  >>> sizeof(int*) is 4 while sizeof(&i) where i is an integer is
  >>> still 8.
  >>> 
  >>> 
  >>> $ cc -g -taso -xtaso_short ptest.c -o ptest $ ./ptest

1.) Use following compiler flags:
 -taso -xtaso

2.) Remove all occurences of "long" in your Sourcecode

3.) Insert:  #pragma pointer_size short
    in your source file.

Maybe have a look to the Migration Guide Manual!!!!
