I am trying to use vdump to backup a disk on a remote 
alpha workstation running Digital Unix V3.2d.

I issue the command:

rsh pipeline /sbin/vdump -0u -f - /usr | dd of=/usr/backup/usr.dump
.
.
vdump: Dumped  1438 of 1438 files; 100.0% completed
vdump: Dump completed at Tue Mar 19 12:00:26 1996
128692+39012 records in
157620+0 records out

I then try to restore from pipeline machine:

rsh tigershark dd if=/usr/backup/usr.dump | /sbin/vrestore -i -f -

I get the following error:


vrestore: unable to use save-set; invalid or corrupt format


Any ideas on why this does not work?

Thanks in advance for your help.

Tom
murray@ans.net



