We have the same problem here. There seems to be information at the end
of the dump file which corrupts the restore/
One solution is to compress the output file and uncompress it before
restore. Compression removes this "dirt" at the end. Don't ask me why,
but it works:
rsh pipeline /sbin/vdump -0u -f - /usr | dd of=/usr/backup/usr.dump 
gzip usr.dump
and then 
gunzip usr.dump.gz before vrestore

MAX

