>Almost all modern unix support COW fork, like Digital UNIX, Linux, ...,etc.
>the only system I use does not support COW fork is ULTRIX.

Minor correction: on some platforms it is not copy-on-write but
copy-on-reference. This is because some architectures (mainly RISC)
have trouble with mapping a physical page to multiple virtual addresses.

The only platform I know for sure does copy-on-reference is HP-UX on the
PA-RISC platform; but I suspect that AIX also does it. Anyone know?

-- Andrew  (andrewg@microlise.co.uk)

